{"name":"Blue Velvet","hex":"#0d6183","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"velvet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A closely woven fabric (originally of silk, now also of cotton or man-made fibres) with a thick short pile on one side.","Very fine fur, including the skin and fur on a deer's antlers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with velvet or with a covering of a similar texture.","To coat raw meat in starch, then in oil, preparatory to frying."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velvet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Velvet (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Blue Velvet\" is a popular song written and composed in 1950 by Bernie Wayne and Lee Morris. A top 20 hit for Tony Bennett in its original 1951 version, the song has since been re-recorded many times, with a 1963 version by Bobby Vinton reaching No. 1."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Velvet_(song)"},{"title":"Blue on Blue (Bobby Vinton album)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue on Blue, later renamed Blue Velvet, is Bobby Vinton's sixth studio album, released in 1963. Cover versions include the jazz songs \"St. Louis Blues\" and \"Blueberry Hill\", \"Am I Blue\", \"Blue, Blue Day\", the Fleetwoods' hit \"Mr. Blue\", \"My Blue Heaven\", three show tunes, and The Clovers Rhythm and blues hit, \"Blue Velvet\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7b/Bluevelvet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_on_Blue_(Bobby_Vinton_album)"},{"title":"Blue Velvet (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Velvet is a 1986 American neo-noir mystery thriller film written and directed by David Lynch. The film stars Kyle MacLachlan, Isabella Rossellini, Dennis Hopper, and Laura Dern, and is named after the 1951 song of the same name. The film follows a college student (MacLachlan) who returns to his hometown and discovers a severed human ear in a field, which leads him to uncover a criminal conspiracy involving a troubled nightclub singer (Rossellini)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fd/Blue_Velvet_%281986%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Velvet_(film)"},{"title":"Velvet","blocks":[{"text":"Velvet is a type of woven fabric with a dense, even pile that gives it a distinctive soft feel. Historically, velvet was typically made from silk. Modern velvet can be made from silk, linen, cotton, wool, synthetic fibers, silk-cotton blends, or synthetic-natural fiber blends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velvet"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b9/Blue_Velvet_Song_Recorde_Single.jpg/250px-Blue_Velvet_Song_Recorde_Single.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b9/Blue_Velvet_Song_Recorde_Single.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b9/Blue_Velvet_Song_Recorde_Single.jpg/250px-Blue_Velvet_Song_Recorde_Single.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Velvet_Song_Recorde_Single.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Lana_Del_Rey_Blue_Velvet_Cover.jpeg/500px-Lana_Del_Rey_Blue_Velvet_Cover.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Lana_Del_Rey_Blue_Velvet_Cover.jpeg/1280px-Lana_Del_Rey_Blue_Velvet_Cover.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Lana_Del_Rey_Blue_Velvet_Cover.jpeg/500px-Lana_Del_Rey_Blue_Velvet_Cover.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALana_Del_Rey_Blue_Velvet_Cover.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/61/Blue_Velvet_1986.jpg/250px-Blue_Velvet_1986.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/61/Blue_Velvet_1986.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/61/Blue_Velvet_1986.jpg/250px-Blue_Velvet_1986.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"I guess it means there's trouble until the robins come\": Throughout the film, a dream Sandy had is alluded to, in which the world was full of darkness and turmoil until a group of robins were set free, unleashing blinding light and love. Lighting is a strong symbolic aspect of the film, illustrated in this second shot which is lit from above before fading out, representing a return to normality.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Velvet_1986.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Isabella_Rossellini_David_Lynch_Cannes.jpg/500px-Isabella_Rossellini_David_Lynch_Cannes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.